{"c":[{"id":"842e4a5a9e2cd880","sum":"B23/W1/W2: recovery.sqlite rows of runs under way return stopped with undo; react-select's chosen input has opacity 0 (walker waives it); an open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; under a held heavy lock accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"685d64f7872e343d","sum":"B23/W2: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way; at start their skills go back on Tab, rows list as stopped with undo, id generators skip ids in use. react-select sets its input opacity 0 once chosen; walker.visibleReactSelect waives opacity there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171834Z-0d54f9ef314f8bad","text":"B23: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way (skill_id in clear). At start each row's skill goes back on Tab; readable rows list as 'Stopped when Caret restarted, at step N of M' with undo. Id generators skip ids in use (idTaken).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-06db563b8bbd4ad9","text":"W2: react-select makes its input opacity 0 whenever a value is chosen, so the walker's opacity rule dropped it; walker.visibleReactSelect waives only opacity inside a visible react-select box.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"224bf2f9191d9b3d","sum":"W1/W2: open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive (360 s, CfT 154); headless CfT registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids reads it. accept.ts: page acceptance; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2154a79bf4058057","text":"W2: headless Chrome for Testing registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids <pid> reads it; accept.ts uses that for the AXManualAccessibility log check (Electron fixture via helper/scripts/electron-setup.sh).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2950b78a7b855fe8","text":"W1: an open connectNative port kept the MV3 worker alive through 360 s idle (same instance, CfT 154). Page acceptance: node fixtures/web-form/accept.ts; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7f5511b9b77cbeaa","sum":"W1/W2/I1: CfT reads NM manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; worker result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields; page.sock key is HMAC(secret,'caret-page-key'); caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + secret; golden lines are indexed 0-based on both sides.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bc66b962416e3ac5","sum":"W1/W2: CfT 154 with --user-data-dir reads NM manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome takes one command-line URL; the worker's result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields, so a new one (choice, attached, pageChanged) goes there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-9a5093647c9001cd","text":"W1: Chrome for Testing 154 with --user-data-dir reads Native Messaging manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome refuses more than one command-line URL; chrome.runtime.getFrameId is undefined in content scripts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-d139eff429d072a1","text":"W2: the worker's result() forwards only named fields of ActAnswer; a new field (choice, attached) must be added there or it silently never reaches the helper.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8a8589948371a0f4","sum":"I1: page.sock key is HMAC(launch secret,'caret-page-key'); bridge needs engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + 32-byte secret on stdin. Golden protocol.ndjson lines 60-68 are indexed 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T183627Z-67627518ce143f34","text":"I1: page.sock's key is HMAC(launch secret, 'caret-page-key') in <sock>.key, and the bridge requires engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; main.ts starts no page.sock without --auth-fd. Since B23, anything that spawns caret-screen must pass --auth-fd 0 and a 32-byte secret on stdin.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183627Z-707cb99ebedd3d58","text":"I1 golden order: protocol.ndjson lines 60-66 are B23's (hello/helperAuth/marks), 67-68 W2's pageEngine; tests index them 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
